4. Interface presets and the C2M template
-----------------------------------------

The 802.3dj C2M preset starts from an 802-COM config template, shipped
unchanged, byte for byte, with its own License Notice sheet:

  sicopr_assist/data/templates/config_com-4p13p0_802p3dj_d2p3_200G_C2M_TP0_TP2_Egress_26_01_27.xlsx
  from opensource.ieee.org/802-com/com_code, tag 4.17.0
  (SHA-256 57e9da3f17dee495f386622f2bab30895a55b2ed40f2df997636d1a73af62e6e)

Every preset value in sicopr_assist/data/presets.csv names its source
(document and clause or table and page, or workbook and cell) in the column
source, and its terms in the column license:

  BSD-3-Clause, 802-COM workbook (Copyright 2025 802-COM Authors)
      values from the 802-COM C2C, CR and C2M templates and from the
      starting workbooks, under their own License Notice

  BSD-3-Clause, standard value under the COM workbook terms
  (Copyright 2025 802-COM Authors)
      COM parameter values taken from IEEE Std 802.3ck-2022, IEEE
      P802.3dj/D2.4, the IEEE COM 3.70 workbooks and the public OIF
      implementation agreement OIF-CEI-05.3. By the maintainer's ruling of
      21 October 2026 these values ship under the same terms as the COM
      configuration workbooks, the License Notice below. The documents
      themselves are not part of SiCoPR-Assist and are not redistributed;
      only the parameter values, each tagged with its source, are. This
      covers COM parameter values only, not channel data or COM results.
      Nothing whose only source is an OIF member working text (the
      CEI-224G MR, VSR and LR drafts) is included.

  BSD-3-Clause, SiCoPR-Assist (Copyright 2026 Todd Bermensolo)
      values SiCoPR-Assist chooses itself: a receiver structure (no Rx FFE,
      no MLSE), a proposal, or N_qb = 0 where the reference stops without
      an Rx FFE

